          "create_time": 1791840930.337,
          "update_time": 1791840932.555,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "I found a substantive problem with Claude’s Newman rationale. The quoted “400×” barrier slack compares the remaining margin with the approximation error; it does not measure slack in the derivative bounds. The derivative allowances are much larger, so a modest underestimate could invalidate a barrier cell. I still favor checking the uniform error budget early, but this ratio does not justify deprioritizing the barrier audit.\n"
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "end_turn": false,
