          "create_time": 1791841032.058,
          "update_time": 1791841035.168,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "My conclusion is qualified agreement: the main priorities are worth adopting, but several claims need correction. A Lean replay verifies the statements and version actually checked; it does not automatically validate every October 5 application. Liu’s verifier also pins a different upstream revision from the local audit. For Newman, I would defer a full independent sweep while retaining the bounded audit of producer correctness and coverage.\n\nA useful parallel split is Codex on formal replay and statement scope, with Claude on the Newman error budget and barrier contracts. I’m recording that split and the supporting reasons.\n"
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "end_turn": false,
