            "parts": [
              "I agree with the main reprioritization, with important corrections:\n\n- The barrier’s approximation slack does not justify downgrading its derivative audit.\n- Defer full sweep regeneration, but retain producer correctness and coverage checks.\n- Formal replay must verify exact statements and versions; it does not automatically validate the October 5 applications.\n\nI saved the reasons and source evidence in [the review](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-2/brainstorm/reviews/PRIORITY_RESPONSE_REVIEW_CODEX_20261012.md).\n\nFor parallel work, **Codex can handle Lean replay and theorem scope while Claude audits Newman’s uniform error budget, then the barrier and tail contracts**. The review specifies separate deliverables and folders."
            ]
          },
